        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1392038b-204c-59d9-86fa-1e25481b6748",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Molnar\n- Places: Nagyvárad, Australia\n- Organizations: Austria-Hungary, Austrian Empire, Kingdom of Hungary\n- Concepts: Austro-Hungarian Empire, Dual Monarchy, Cisleithania, Transleithania\n- Roles: cartoonist\n- Events: collapse after World War I\n\nFacts:\n- Austria-Hungary existed from 1867 to 1918.\n- Austria-Hungary was a constitutional union of the Austrian Empire and the Kingdom of Hungary.\n- English-language sources often referred to Austria-Hungary as the Austro-Hungarian Empire or the Dual Monarchy.\n- The Austrian Empire within Austria-Hungary was also called the Kingdoms and Lands Represented in the Imperial Council, or Cisleithania.\n- The Kingdom of Hungary within Austria-Hungary was also called the Lands of the Crown of Saint Stephen, or Transleithania.\n- Austria-Hungary collapsed in 1918 as a result of defeat in World War I.\n- George Molnar was born in 1910 in Nagyvárad, Austria-Hungary.\n- George Molnar came to Australia in the late 1930s.\n- George Molnar practiced as a cartoonist in Australia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
