        "text": "Page: George Molnar. Sentence: George Molnar (1910–1998) was born in Nagyvárad, Austria-Hungary but came to Australia in the late 1930s, where he practiced as a cartoonist.\nPage: Austria-Hungary. Sentence: Austria-Hungary, often referred to as the Austro-Hungarian Empire or the Dual Monarchy in English-language sources, was a constitutional union of the Austrian Empire (the Kingdoms and Lands Represented in the Imperial Council, or \"Cisleithania\") and the Kingdom of Hungary (Lands of the Crown of Saint Stephen or \"Transleithania\") that existed from 1867 to 1918, when it collapsed as a result of defeat in World War I.",
